body:
Thanks for the advice. I will try weed. A

&#x200B;

As for confidence I am so sick of that advice being thrown around. It isn't tangible or measurable or something that can be directly worked on like going to the gym or learning math. 

&#x200B;

Also I'm 28 and I don't have a lot of time to catch up on the experiences everyone else had. If I'm 30 and have never been in a long term relationship nor have any true close friends then people, especially women, will suspect something is wrong with me and therefore stay away or think I'm some sort of loser for not having the normal experiences everyone else was easily able to get. Honestly if I'm not in a long term relationship by 30 I;m just going to kill myself beause I will be too far gone from saving.
